# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF.
#
# The repository is already LF in the index throughout. Git for Windows sets
# core.autocrlf=true by default, which checks these files out as CRLF. That is
# harmless for the Python files, but not for the ones that are mounted into the
# Linux containers: the *.sh scripts break outright, and docker/.env and
# docker/pgadmin-pgpass would carry a stray carriage return into a password.
#
# Pinning eol=lf here wins over core.autocrlf, so every clone gets the same files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Notebooks are JSON with embedded output. Merging them by line never produces
# something Jupyter can open, so conflicts have to be resolved by hand.
*.ipynb -merge

# Images are never converted. Git detects this on its own, but being explicit
# means a future change to the line above cannot corrupt them.
*.jpg binary
